     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily with meals. The maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and it gives no added glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you have in mind\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
      }
